summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Right heel pain.

MEDICAL HISTORY

The patient is a 30-year-old male who presents for evaluation of right heel pain.

SOCIAL HISTORY

The patient is training for a triathlon and notes that the pain in the back of his heel is present after activity and also in the morning. He notes that it is worse when he first gets up out of bed. He is an aggressive trainer, running 10 km in the morning, biking for 45-60 minutes at lunch, and swimming 30-60 minutes in the evening 5 days a week.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Musculoskeletal: Reports right heel pain.

PHYSICAL EXAM

MSK: Examination of the lower extremities: Right heel pain to palpation of the Achilles tendon. Pain to squeeze of the Achilles tendon. No pain to squeeze of the left calf. Positive Thompson test on the right. Pain to palpation of the right Achilles tendon.

ASSESSMENT

Achilles tendinitis.

PLAN

The patient was advised to stop training for a week or two. He was prescribed Ibuprofen 3 tablets every 6 hours. He will have a couple of physical therapy visits. He will follow up with me in 7-10 days.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will continue to take Ibuprofen 3 tablets every 6 hours. He will follow up with me in 7-10 days. }}<|eot_id|>
