I explained to the patient that I believe he has carpal tunnel syndrome. I explained that this is a common condition that is caused by compression of the median nerve in the wrist. I explained that the compression is caused by thickening of the tendons and ligaments in the wrist. I explained that this compression causes numbness, tingling, and pain in the hand. I explained that the pain is worse with wrist extension and flexion. I explained that the numbness and tingling are mostly constant and worse in the thumb, index, and middle fingers. I explained that the other two fingers are normal. I explained that the pain is worse with typing on the keyboard and mouse. I explained that the pain is not at night and is not affecting his sleep. I explained that the pain is improved with ibuprofen and stopping typing. I explained that I am going to order an EMG to confirm the diagnosis. I explained that if the EMG is positive, we will start with conservative treatment. If the EMG is negative, we will continue with conservative treatment. If the EMG is positive and conservative treatment does not improve the symptoms, we will consider surgery.

Patient Agreements

The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient was instructed to wear a wrist splint at night. The patient was instructed to continue with ibuprofen 600 mg 4 times a day. The patient was instructed to return in 2 weeks for a follow up appointment. }}<|eot_id|>
